/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 66 0 R
/T (1. Introduction and Product Evolution The technological shift in submersible pumping systems reached a critical milestone in 1995 with the introduction of u-PVC Column Pipes. Prior to this, Galvanized Iron \(GI\) pipes were the industry standard; however, the engineering community recognized a significant need for materials offering higher tensile load sustainability and superior resistance to chemical degradation. The transition from GI to the Prayag Boretec u-PVC system is underpinned by the material's high hydrostatic pressure resistance and its ability to sustain the constant jerks and vertical loads inherent in deep-well submersible applications. Unlike traditional iron pipes, this system ensures the delivery of clean, uncontaminated water throughout its operational lifespan.)
/E (1. Introduction and Product Evolution The technological shift in submersible pumping systems reached a critical milestone in 1995 with the introduction of u-PVC Column Pipes. Prior to this, Galvanized Iron \(GI\) pipes were the industry standard; however, the engineering community recognized a significant need for materials offering higher tensile load sustainability and superior resistance to chemical degradation. The transition from GI to the Prayag Boretec u-PVC system is underpinned by the material's high hydrostatic pressure resistance and its ability to sustain the constant jerks and vertical loads inherent in deep-well submersible applications. Unlike traditional iron pipes, this system ensures the delivery of clean, uncontaminated water throughout its operational lifespan.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
